+### 0.x 🌐 Translation drift: what is yours and what is inherited
+
+`Docs Sync (Strict)` is **PR-scoped since 2026-10-20**: on a pull request `check-translation-drift.mjs
+--base-report` fails only on drift the PR introduces; drift the base already carried is printed as
+inherited. The push run and the nightly Release-Green keep the full strict verdict, so a red
+`release/vX+1` tip for translation drift is the **i18n wave's** debt (`/i18n-waves`), not something a
+release fix PR or the sync-back may "repair" by adopting hashes. Before the freeze, read the nightly's
+drift list and ask the owner for the wave (or the backend credentials/balance it needs) — do not carry
+14 drifted sources into the release expecting the squash to clear them (v3.8.52 shipped that way).
